  "title": "Total positivity of order four for the Eulerian triangle: an exact computer-assisted proof",
  "batch_label": "42",
  "kind": "resolution-paper",
  "original_status": "proved",
  "scope": "Let A(n,k) count permutations of [n+1] with k descents and be zero outside 0<=k<=n. For every 1<=s<=4 and strictly increasing nonnegative row and column tuples n_1<...<n_s and k_1<...<k_s, det[A(n_i,k_j)] is nonnegative. More strongly, every admissible minor of order at most four (k_i<=n_i for each aligned index) is strictly positive, while every nonadmissible minor is zero.",
  "gate_basis": "Current released terminal, manifest, PDF, TeX freeze, snapshot files, provenance and four audits agree.",
